How the book is organised
Part I covers what you need first: what Quarto does (1  Publishing That Rebuilds Itself), how to work with a coding agent safely (2  Working With a Coding Agent), how to set up your computer (3  Setting Up Your Machine), and a first report made by hand (4  A First Report, by Hand), in which you render it, check it against its data, record it with Git and undo a change yourself before an agent makes one. The GitHub account it asks for is free; an agent’s account may not be. Claude Code, for one, needs a paid plan or pay-per-use billing (checked 2026-11-18; Before you start lists what each agent needs). Parts II and III build the two projects, with the statistics explained on the way, and each ends by changing an input and explaining what the rebuild changed. The afterword offers three projects that carry the method into your own work, a metrics brief, a research supplement and a coursework report, each rebuilt from a fresh copy of its repository (Afterword). The appendices hold the Windows setup, the terminal’s keys and habits, a cheatsheet, troubleshooting, every checkpoint, the data sources and how this book is built.
By the end of the book you will be able to:

explain how Quarto turns one source into many formats, and why every rebuild gives the same result;
direct a coding agent safely: a folder of its own, written rules, and one step per prompt, each ending in a check;
build and publish both projects, the London guide and the water-risk website, each in several formats;
predict which outputs a changed input will update, and check that the rebuild did exactly that.

explain how Quarto turns one plain-text source into many formats, and why a computed number cannot drift from its data;
direct a coding agent safely, with written rules, one task per prompt and a check after each;
build and publish a site from data for several readers, as you did for London and for the water analysis;
read an agent’s change with git diff before you keep it, and undo one with git restore;
predict which outputs a changed input or setting updates, rebuild, and explain the result;
say which edition of this book shows each interactive figure, and why.
